course: dictionary
lesson: 10366
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Travelling can do different jobs in a sentence. As a verb, it shows an action, like «The Rat has never been further than the ring of Downs» in one story, where a travelling Sea Rat tells him about far-off voyages. Look at the words around it to find its job.
explain: In a ball game, «You can't run while holding the ball (travelling)» means moving with the ball in a way the rules do not allow. The sentence tells you what travelling means here: running with the ball is against the rules, so it is a foul.
explain: As an adjective, travelling describes a thing. «A travelling show» is a show that moves from place to place. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «a show that moves from place to place» still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Travelling means going from one place to another, especially far away, on a trip or journey.
fact: Travelling can also be a noun: it is the activity of going on journeys.
fact: As an adjective, travelling means moving from place to place, like a travelling circus.
fact: «Travelling sickness» means car sickness, the feeling of being unwell while in a moving vehicle.
fact: In science, travelling can mean moving through space, as in «light travelling through glass».
exercise: «You can't run while holding the ball (travelling).» In this sentence, what does travelling mean? | Passing the ball quickly to a friend | Sleeping on the bench | *Moving with the ball in a way the rules do not allow | Scoring a goal from far away
exercise: What does «a travelling show» mean? | A show that is cancelled | A show that stays in one place all year | A very long show | *A show that moves from place to place
exercise: In «light travelling through glass», what is travelling? | Shining brightly in a room | Sitting still | Breaking into pieces | *Moving through space
test: «You buy a ticket before boarding, because travelling without one can mean a fine.» What does travelling without one mean? | Buying a ticket for a friend | Waiting at a bus stop | *Going on a journey with no ticket | Checking the time on a clock
test: Which job does travelling do in «Travelling is fun for everyone»? | Preposition: showing place | Adjective: describing a thing | *Noun: the activity of going on journeys | Verb: showing an action now
exam: Which word is a noun in «Travelling is fun for everyone»? | everyone | is | *Travelling | fun
